  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we walk to the pond in the park. Britain is full of water, and the five birds in this lesson live on almost all of it: from the canal in town to the lake in the country park.\n\nWater birds are the perfect place to train your eye. They are big, they sit still, and they let you look closely. We start with the most familiar duck in the country and end with a bird that can stand still for half an hour.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of eight questions, with two birds from last week mixed in."
  },
